# Racketeer Boss (racketeer_boss.txt): its ETB lets you choose a creature
# card in hand, which perpetually gains "When you cast this spell, create a
# Treasure token and this spell perpetually loses this ability" (ADR-0023's
# trigger grant, Duration$ Perpetual). The grant survives hand -> stack,
# fires from the stack (CR 603.2, a spell's own cast trigger) and
# LosePerpetual strips it, so recasting the card makes no second Treasure.
startturn human
advance 3
# Cast Racketeer Boss; its ETB chooses Grizzly Bears (Id:2) in hand.
tapformana human 3 R
tapformana human 4 G
queue cardchoice 2
castspell human 1
resolvestack
# Cast Grizzly Bears: the granted trigger makes a Treasure, then loses itself.
tapformana human 5 G
tapformana human 6 G
queue paygeneric G
castspell human 2
resolvestack
# Shatterstorm destroys that Treasure (a token ceases to exist, CR 704.5d),
# so any Treasure left at the end would be a second one.
tapformana human 7 R
tapformana human 8 R
tapformana human 9 R
tapformana human 10 R
queue paygeneric R
queue paygeneric R
castspell human 14
resolvestack
# Unsummon returns the Bears to hand; recasting them triggers nothing.
tapformana human 11 U
queue targets 2
castspell human 15
resolvestack
tapformana human 12 G
tapformana human 13 G
queue paygeneric G
castspell human 2
resolvestack
